._*
.DS_Store
coverage
dist
node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo

# A test fixture may legitimately be called `dist`. The rule above is
# unanchored, so it matches at any depth, and `discover/built-app` is a fixture
# whose whole point is a `bin` naming built output the way a real package does
# -- `dist/cli.mjs` is the realistic spelling and is the thing under test.
#
# Left ignored the fixture is simply absent from a clone, so every test passes
# for whoever generated it once and fails for everybody else. That is how CI
# went red on `main`, and the failure says `Entry module not found`, which
# points at the discovery code rather than at the missing file.
#
# The directory is re-included before its contents, because git does not
# descend into an excluded directory to find a negation inside it.
#
# `node_modules` is deliberately NOT re-included: the only fixture files under
# one are `.sigil/entry.mjs`, which is what `sigil build` writes, and generated
# output does not belong in the repo.
!packages/*/test/fixtures/**/dist/
!packages/*/test/fixtures/**/dist/**
